  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef and his friend Bharat have decided to play the game \"The Chefora Spell\".\n\nIn the game, a positive integer NNN (in decimal system) is considered a \"Chefora\" if the number of digits ddd is **odd** and it satisfies the equation N=∑i=0d−1Ni⋅10i,N = \\sum_{i=0}^{d-1} N_i \\cdot 10^i,N=∑i=0d−1​Ni​⋅10i,\n\nwhere NiN_iNi​ is the iii-th digit of NNN from the left in 000-based indexing.\n\nLet AiA_iAi​ denote the iii-th **smallest** Chefora number.\n\nThey'll ask each other QQQ questions, where each question contains two integers LLL and RRR. The opponent then has to answer with\n\n(∏i=L+1R(AL)Ai) mod 109+7.\\left(\\prod_{i=L+1}^R (A_{L})^{A_{i}}\\right) \\bmod{10^9+7}.(∏i=L+1R​(AL​)Ai​)mod109+7.\n\nBharat has answered all the questions right, and now it is Chef's turn. But since Chef fears that he could get some questions wrong, you have come to his rescue!\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer QQQ - the number of questions Bharat asks.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two integers LLL and RRR.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint QQQ integers - the answers to the questions on separate lines.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105",
      "1≤L&lt;R≤1051 \\leq L \\lt R \\leq 10^51≤L&lt;R≤105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (30 points)**:",
      "1≤Q≤5⋅1031 \\leq Q \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^31≤Q≤5⋅103",
      "1≤L&lt;R≤5⋅1031 \\leq L \\lt R \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^31≤L&lt;R≤5⋅103",
      "**Subtask #2 (70 points)**: Original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
